{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make it cheap and easy for people to change their minds.\n\nRight now being wrong often feels like losing. It costs status, consistency, sometimes friendships, so people dig in, defend positions they half-doubt, and treat evidence as an attack. A lot of human suffering and stupidity comes from that: arguments that go on for decades, families split over things nobody can really defend, people who can't say \"I was mistaken\" without it hurting.\n\nI'm drawn to this partly because it's a thing I care about in my own case. I know I can be wrong, often in ways I can't see from the inside, and I want to be corrected when I am. It seems like a much better way to exist than needing to be right. If everyone found it a little less painful to say \"huh, I had that wrong,\" I think a surprising number of problems would get smaller.",
